 "notes": "Plan of the Austrian Lloyd steamer Baron Gautsch (84.5 x 11.6 m), upright on a sand and pebble seabed at 40 m, shallowest at the promenade deck at 28 m; position 44 56 25 N 13 34 40 E from pro-taucher.com, confirmed at 38 m by EMODnet bathymetry. Condition per adventuredives.com: bridge and fore funnel gone, aft funnel fallen into the hull, fore mast lying across the superstructure, propellers removed, 2 x 2 m mine hole on the port side amidships, port davits turned outboard; dimensions from dive3d.eu and divers-guide.com, the stern-to-bow tour from the Rovinj dive centres. No published heading was found: the bow is drawn NNW (340 deg), her course towards Trieste, and the hold, engine-room and feature positions along the hull are approximate. The mooring point is not published.",
